2. FIX PREMIUM AI RESPONSE FORMATTING

A. Fix the Literal Markdown Bug

The current Study Buddy response visibly displays strings such as:

- "**Revisions Due Today:**"
- "**Scheduled Tasks Today:**"
- "**Morning**"
- "**Pick 1 Chapter to Start:**"

This is a rendering defect. Markdown formatting syntax is being displayed as literal text instead of being rendered correctly.

Inspect the actual message rendering pipeline and identify the root cause.

Determine whether the backend returns Markdown, the frontend expects plain text, Markdown is escaped twice, or a custom parser is incorrectly processing the content.

Implement a consistent, safe rendering strategy.

Requirements:

- Bold Markdown must render as actual bold text.
- Headings must have appropriate hierarchy.
- Bulleted and numbered lists must display correctly.
- Paragraphs must have comfortable spacing.
- Inline code and code blocks must render correctly when relevant.
- Links must be rendered safely and be tappable when appropriate.
- Tables must either render correctly on mobile or be transformed into a mobile-friendly alternative.
- Unordered and ordered lists must not lose their structure.
- Preserve line breaks where meaningful.
- Handle malformed or incomplete Markdown gracefully.

Do not simply remove all asterisks with a string replacement. Do not destroy legitimate text, punctuation, lists, or formatting.

Choose an implementation appropriate for the actual framework already used in the project.

If the project uses Jetpack Compose, use an appropriate Compose-compatible rendering approach or a well-tested lightweight Markdown renderer. If it uses XML-based Android views, WebView, or another framework, follow the existing architecture and use a suitable solution.

Do not add a heavy dependency unless necessary.

